    '{"\$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","\$id":"https://trusttasks.org/spec/hcp/grants/list/0.1","title":"HCP — List Grants — payload","description":"The request payload of the HCP 2.0-draft-3 List grants operation (HCP 5.4, 6.1.5; `GET /v2/grants` with a Management Client\'s token in HCP 9.4.6): a Management Client, acting for the Authorizing Principal, enumerates the grants for the instance, filtered by status. HCP defines no request schema for this operation; the members come from HCP 9.4.6 (`status`) and 9.5 (`cursor`, `limit`). The outer document members (id, type, issuer, recipient, issuedAt, expiresAt, proof) are owned by the framework — SPEC §6.3. Every maxLength, maxItems and maxProperties in this schema is a Trust Tasks framework bound (SPEC §7.3 item 19), not an HCP requirement; so is every minLength or minItems of 1 on a member HCP\'s own schema allows to be empty.","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"status":{"type":"string","enum":["active","revoked","expired"],"description":"HCP\'s `status` query parameter (HCP 9.4.6): list only grants with this status (HCP 6.1.5). Absent means `active`, HCP\'s default; HCP offers no value for every status. HCP\'s own values, carried verbatim."},"cursor":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":2048,"description":"HCP\'s `cursor` query parameter (HCP 9.5): the opaque continuation token from a prior response\'s `nextCursor`. Absent means the first page. The maxLength is a framework bound, not an HCP requirement."},"limit":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":1000,"description":"HCP\'s `limit` query parameter (HCP 9.5): the most grants in this page. Absent means the provider\'s own page size. The maximum of 1000 is a framework bound, not an HCP requirement."},"accessToken":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":8192,"description":"The Management Client\'s HCP access token (HCP 9.3), carried unchanged. HCP\'s HTTP Binding sends it as a Bearer token; this member carries it in the document. The provider validates it exactly as over HTTP and treats it as opaque. A Context Client\'s token is answered with that client\'s own grant only, as over HCP\'s HTTP Binding (HCP 9.4.6; pending HCP confirmation, question 19). The maxLength is a framework bound, not an HCP requirement. OPTIONAL: where it is absent, the provider authenticates the request\'s `issuer` VID, by the REQUIRED request proof, as a Management Client the Authorizing Principal enrolled (HCP 3.2.3), and refuses any other issuer with permissionDenied; where it is present, the token rules apply unchanged. Pending HCP confirmation (question 56)."}}}';

/// As [payloadSchemaJson], for the success-response variant.
const String responsePayloadSchemaJson =
    '{"\$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","\$ref":"#/\$defs/Response","\$defs":{"Response":{"\$anchor":"response","title":"HCP — List Grants — response payload","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["grants"],"description":"A page of grant objects (HCP 6.1.5, 9.4.6), with the cursor for the next page where there is one (HCP 9.5). Failures use trust-task-error, not this shape.","properties":{"grants":{"type":"array","maxItems":1000,"items":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Grant"},"description":"The grants with the status asked for, `active` by default (HCP 9.4.6), each a grant object (HCP 6.1.5). Empty where there are none. The maxItems, the carriage\'s cap on `limit`, is a framework bound, not an HCP requirement."},"nextCursor":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":2048,"description":"HCP `nextCursor` (HCP 9.5): an opaque token for the next page, valid for at least 300 seconds, encoding no credential and no entry content. Absent when the set is exhausted, where HCP\'s HTTP Binding sends null. The maxLength is a framework bound, not an HCP requirement."}}},"Grant":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true,"required":["grantId","subject","authorizingPrincipal","client","access","grantType","issuedAt","expiresAt","status"],"description":"A grant (HCP 6.1.5). `expiresAt` is an instant for a `temporary` grant and null for a `persistent` one (HCP 6.1.4, 6.1.5). That rule is stated here and not as a schema conditional: the registry\'s Rust generator does not support `if`/`then`/`else`, so it is not checked by the schema. An HCP Provider never discloses a grant issued to one HCP Client to any other (HCP 6.1.5).","properties":{"grantId":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Urn","description":"Stable for the life of the grant; the `grantId` recorded in audit events (HCP 6.1.5, 8.2)."},"subject":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/GrantParty","description":"The Context Subject, by a pseudonym specific to the client (HCP 3.4)."},"authorizingPrincipal":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/AuthorizingPrincipal","description":"Who authorized the grant (HCP 3.4, 6.1.5)."},"client":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/GrantClient","description":"The HCP Client the grant was issued to (HCP 6.1.5)."},"requestingParty":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/RequestingParty","description":"The party on whose behalf the client requested access, where there is one (HCP 3.2.7, 3.4)."},"access":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"items":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/AccessDetail"},"description":"What the grant authorizes: one or more authorization details (HCP 6.1.5)."},"scopes":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","maxLength":2048,"pattern":"^hcp:[^:]+(:[^:]+)*:(read|write)\$"},"description":"Scope strings derived from `access`, in the form `hcp:{category}:{action}` (HCP 6.1.1), for display. They never grant anything `access` does not (HCP 6.1.5)."},"grantType":{"type":"string","enum":["temporary","persistent"],"description":"Temporary or persistent (HCP 6.1.4). HCP\'s own values, carried verbatim."},"issuedAt":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Instant","description":"When the grant was issued."},"expiresAt":{"type":["string","null"],"format":"date-time","description":"For a temporary grant, its absolute expiry, never null; for a persistent grant, null (HCP 6.1.4, 6.1.5)."},"status":{"type":"string","enum":["active","revoked","expired"],"description":"`expired` on lapse of `expiresAt`, `revoked` on revocation (HCP 6.1.5, 6.2.1). HCP\'s own values, carried verbatim."}}},"AccessDetail":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true,"required":["type","actions","categories","purposes"],"description":"An authorization detail (HCP 6.1.5); under HCP\'s OAuth Interop Profile, an RFC 9396 authorization detail (HCP 13.3). `onwardSharing` appears only in a detail that includes `read` and all of whose categories have a default sensitivity of Low (HCP 6.1.5); not checked by the schema.","properties":{"type":{"type":"string","const":"https://hcp.example/spec/authorization/context-access","description":"The HCP authorization detail type (HCP 6.1.5)."},"actions":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"uniqueItems":true,"items":{"type":"string","enum":["read","write","provenance"]},"description":"What the detail allows. `provenance` is an action only alongside `read` (HCP 6.1.5, 7.4.1); not checked by the schema."},"categories":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"uniqueItems":true,"items":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Category"},"description":"The categories the detail covers (HCP 4.5)."},"purposes":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"items":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Purpose"},"description":"The purposes the person approved for these categories; never empty (HCP 6.1.5.2)."},"narrowedTo":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true,"description":"An implementation-defined narrowing below category grain, which only narrows (HCP 6.1.5.1). To a Context Client, entries it names are named by `ref`, never by `id` (HCP 5.2.6)."},"onwardSharing":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/OnwardSharing","description":"The onward sharing the person elected for the detail (HCP 3.12, 6.1.5)."}}},"OnwardSharing":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true,"description":"Present only where the Authorizing Principal elected onward sharing for the detail (HCP 3.12, 6.1.5).","properties":{"domains":{"type":"array","uniqueItems":true,"items":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":253},"description":"Where present, the DNS domains of the organizations the client may share with (HCP 6.1.5)."},"notTo":{"type":"array","uniqueItems":true,"items":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":2048},"description":"Set by the provider: each DNS domain or operator a standing rule denies any of the detail\'s categories (HCP 6.1.5, 6.3)."}}},"Purpose":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true,"required":["code","description"],"description":"A purpose with a description the person can read (HCP 6.1.5.2).","properties":{"code":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/PurposeCode","description":"The purpose code."},"description":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":4096,"description":"The description shown to the person before approval (HCP 6.1.5.2, 6.1.6)."}}},"PurposeCode":{"type":"string","format":"uri","minLength":1,"maxLength":2048,"pattern":"^[a-zA-Z][a-zA-Z0-9+.-]*:\\\\S+\$","description":"An HCP purpose code: an absolute URI naming the purpose for which context is requested or may be used (HCP 6.1.5.2)."},"Category":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":2048,"pattern":"^([a-z][a-z0-9_]*|[a-zA-Z][a-zA-Z0-9+.-]*:\\\\S+)\$","description":"An HCP context category (HCP 4.5), the primary unit of access control: either a slug from HCP\'s category registry, such as `general_preferences` or `health_context`, or a custom category written as an absolute URI under a domain its definer controls. A custom category is not portable between providers without bilateral agreement (HCP 4.5). The pattern admits the slug or an absolute URI\'s outline only: it carries no `format: uri`, which would refuse every slug, so checking that a custom value is a well-formed absolute URI, as HCP\'s prose requires (HCP A.3), is the consumer\'s check."},"RequestingParty":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true,"required":["type","id"],"description":"The Requesting Party (HCP 3.2.7).","properties":{"type":{"type":"string","enum":["person","organization"],"description":"A person or an organization. HCP\'s own values, carried verbatim."},"id":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":2048,"description":"Its identifier."},"name":{"type":"string","maxLength":1024,"description":"Its name."}}},"GrantClient":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true,"required":["id","name","operator"],"description":"The client a grant was issued to (HCP 6.1.5).","properties":{"id":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":2048,"description":"Its client identifier."},"name":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":1024,"description":"A name the person can recognize (HCP 6.1.5)."},"operator":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Named","description":"The Client Operator (HCP 3.2.8)."},"legalRetention":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/LegalRetention","description":"Present only where the client declared a legal obligation to keep what it receives (HCP 6.2.5)."},"claims":{"type":"array","uniqueItems":true,"items":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Uri"},"description":"The client conformance claims it declared at registration (HCP 18.1); absent where it declared none."}}},"LegalRetention":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true,"required":["record","obligation","period"],"description":"A record the client declared at registration that the law requires it to keep of what it receives (HCP 6.2.5).","properties":{"record":{"type":"string","maxLength":4096,"description":"The record kept."},"obligation":{"type":"string","maxLength":4096,"description":"The law or rule that requires it."},"period":{"type":"string","maxLength":1024,"description":"How long it is kept."}}},"Named":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true,"required":["id","name"],"description":"An organization, by identifier and a name a person can recognize.","properties":{"id":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":2048,"description":"Its identifier."},"name":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":1024,"description":"Its name. The minLength is a framework bound, not an HCP requirement."}}},"Uri":{"type":"string","format":"uri","minLength":1,"maxLength":2048,"pattern":"^[a-zA-Z][a-zA-Z0-9+.-]*:\\\\S+\$","description":"An absolute URI with no whitespace, as HCP writes every custom value at an extension point (HCP A.3)."},"AuthorizingPrincipal":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true,"required":["id"],"description":"The Authorizing Principal (HCP 3.4). In Core it is the Context Subject and carries the same pseudonym as `subject`; under the Delegated Authorization Profile it is the delegate (HCP 17.4).","properties":{"id":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":2048,"description":"Its identifier."},"delegation":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":2048,"description":"The delegation under which a delegate authorized the grant; present only then (HCP 6.1.5, 17.4)."}}},"GrantParty":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true,"required":["id"],"description":"An actor a grant binds, named by identifier (HCP 3.4).","properties":{"id":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":2048,"description":"Its identifier; for the Context Subject, a pseudonym specific to the client (HCP 3.4). The minLength is a framework bound, not an HCP requirement."}}},"Instant":{"type":"string","format":"date-time","description":"An RFC 3339 instant."},"Urn":{"type":"string","pattern":"^urn:uuid:[0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12}\$","description":"An HCP identifier: a UUID in `urn:uuid:` form, of any UUID version (HCP 4.2), as HCP uses for entry, grant, directive and retrieval identifiers."}}}';

/// The SPEC §7.2 policy for the request variant, taken from this
/// specification's front matter.
///
/// Pass it to [consumeInbound] — items 5b, 7 and 8 are per-specification and
/// cannot be derived from the document alone, and item 2 needs the schema it
/// carries.
const SpecPolicy spec = SpecPolicy(
  typeUri: typeUri,
  isBearer: false,
  isProofRequired: true,
  isRecipientRequired: true,
  isIssuedAtRequired: true,
  payloadSchema: payloadSchemaJson,
);

/// The SPEC §7.2 policy for the success-response variant.
///
/// `isRecipientRequired` tracks the *issuer* party's requirement, because a
/// response swaps the parties (§7.3 item 5).
const SpecPolicy responseSpec = SpecPolicy(
  typeUri: responseTypeUri,
  isBearer: false,
  isProofRequired: false,
  isRecipientRequired: true,
  isIssuedAtRequired: true,
  payloadSchema: responsePayloadSchemaJson,
  maxDocumentBytes: 4194304,
);
